# Git history for desktop Vaults

LiveSync owns file delivery. Git is version history only.

- All desktops may create automatic snapshots through the coordinated historian.
- Only one device may hold the distributed Git lease at a time.
- Git fetch may update metadata, but Git pull must never overwrite Vault files.
- Exclude `workspace*.json`, credentials, `.LLMHub/rag`, caches and runtime state.
- The iPhone does not run Git; the first online desktop records its LiveSync changes.

